# Project Architecture

## Stack
- **Frontend**: Vite + React 18 + TypeScript
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v3 + CSS custom properties (HSL design tokens in `index.css`)
- **UI Primitives**: Radix UI (no shadcn CLI — components hand-rolled in `src/components/atoms/`)
- **Routing**: React Router v6
- **Backend**: Supabase (Auth + PostgreSQL + RLS + RPC functions)
- **Toasts**: Sonner (`toast.success / toast.error`)
- **Dates**: date-fns (all date helpers live in `src/lib/utils.ts`)

## Folder Structure

```
src/
├── components/
│   ├── atoms/        # Primitive, stateless UI: Button, Input, Badge, Card, Dialog, Select…
│   ├── molecules/    # Composed from atoms: SearchBar, BookCard, StatCard, FormField, EmptyState…
│   ├── organisms/    # Feature-level: Sidebar, Header, NotificationBell
│   └── templates/   # Page shells: DashboardLayout (wraps Outlet)
├── context/          # React context only — AuthContext (user, profile, role, sign in/out)
├── hooks/            # Data-fetching hooks: useBooks, useMembers, useBorrows, useReservations
├── lib/              # supabase.ts (client init), utils.ts (cn, formatDate, etc.)
├── pages/            # One folder per feature: auth/, books/, members/, borrowing/, reservations/, dashboard/
├── services/         # One file per domain: bookService, borrowService, memberService…
└── types/            # database.ts — all TypeScript types mirroring DB schema
supabase/migrations/  # Ordered SQL files: 001_initial_schema, 002_seed_genres, 003_rpc_functions
```

## Layer Rules
- **Pages** orchestrate — they call hooks/services and compose organisms/molecules. No raw `supabase` calls in pages.
- **Services** own all Supabase queries. Return typed domain objects, throw on error.
- **Hooks** call services, manage loading/error state, expose `refetch`.
- **Atoms** are pure UI — no business logic, no service calls.
- **Context** holds only global auth state. Feature data stays in hooks.

## Roles
- `member` — default for all registrations
- `librarian` — manually set in Supabase dashboard (`profiles.role`)
- Role is a PostgreSQL enum `public.user_role ('member' | 'librarian')`
- Use `useAuth().isLibrarian` to gate UI. Use RLS policies to gate data.
